            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to lead to, then the Persian for to conclude."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: به دلیل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به دلیل (be dalil-e) — \"because of, due to\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جاده به دلیل برف بسته شد. jâdde be dalil-e barf baste shod. The road was closed because of snow."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Takes a noun with ezafe; with a clause, be dalil-e inke …."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به دلیل (be dalil-e) joins the Persian preposition be to dalil, from Arabic dalīl (EtymDB glosses it \"guide\"): by reason of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
